<title>INDIA: India soybean steady, truck strike slows arrivals.</title>
<headline>India soybean steady, truck strike slows arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean and soyoil prices stayed steady in thin central Indian markets as arrivals remained poor due to a continuing nationwide truck strike.</p>
<p>Soybean arrivals were around 1,000 tonnes, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil business was slow, and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were easy. Soymeal yellow was $317 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $118 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 4,200 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was at lowest level and the undertone was steady.</p>
